  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thai sweetcorn fritters serve 4 as a snack and take about 22 minutes. The main ingredient is sweetcorn (no slug, use 300 g of drained tinned sweetcorn or kernels cut from 2 fresh cobs). It is bound with beaten "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "eggs",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "eggs"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "cornflour",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "cornflour"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The dipping sauce uses "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "lime",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "lime"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "fish sauce",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fish-sauce"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Shallow-fry in batches for a crisp result."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The batter should be thick enough to hold its shape when spooned into the pan. If it runs and spreads, add another tablespoon of cornflour and stir well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
